==Enemy==
Wicked Face has much longer range than The Face (enough to hit [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]]), which is further increased by his guaranteed [[Mini-Wave]]s. His stats are nothing to sneeze at either, plus he has a 30% chance to [[freeze]] units that survive his attacks, though very briefly. Yet another problem he poses is his [[Shield]], which more than doubles his health while blocking status effects. Fortunately, his movement speed is only double that of The Face and he still has a relatively slow attack rate.

==Strategy==
Because of his range and Mini-Waves, it is quite difficult to properly outrange him, but not impossible. Since both the damage and the freeze uptime are low, most units who outranges him can still do a fairly good job against him while being mildly threatened at worst, or while being protected by [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] at best, who can safely tank Wicked Face's damage, despite him not being a [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy. This works due to Wicked Face's slow attack rate, meaning it will take a while to destroy Octopus Cat or any melee attackers you're using.

Another valid strategy, which is faster in absence of interferences and arguably much more accessible involves bulky units getting up close and quickly dealing damage, all while realistically lasting for a long time while under fire. Some accessible non-[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] options include a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Li'l Titan Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Jamiera]]/[[Li'l Gross Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Macho Legs]], [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]], or even [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]].

Shield aside, little can be done by applying effects on this foe, so raw power, as is often customary with Aku enemies, is the way to go.

